# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession draft Enchanting --out` from Forever's client tables, trainer lists and data/forever. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/enchanting
title Enchanting 1-300
category Professions
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Enchanting turns magic items into enchanting materials (Disenchant: any green or better item gives
# dust, essence or a shard by its level) and puts enchantments on gear. It needs no gathering
# profession: the dust and essence come from disenchanting what you loot, or from the Auction House.
# Each tier needs a runed rod in your bags (Copper, Silver, Golden, Truesilver, Arcanite); the rod
# bases come from blacksmiths or trade vendors.
#
# Forever's changes: the first levels run on Mote of Magic, 10c at enchanting supply vendors with no
# stock limit. Runed Copper Rod is a Copper Rod and 1 Mote; Bracer - Inferior Stamina (Classic's
# Minor Health) takes 1 Mote and goes grey at 25; Dust to Motes turns 1 Strange Dust into 3 Motes.
# Strange Dust and Lesser Magic Essence are still sold, but only 1 to 4 at a time, so this route
# runs on the Strange Dust that low-level greens break into (Chest - Inferior Stamina, then Cloak -
# Minor Protection). Several later formulas need fewer materials (Runed Silver Rod: 3 Strange Dust
# and 4 Lesser Magic Essence). New formulas for caster weapons, relics and necklaces are sold for
# Merchant's Favor by Beneris near the Crossroads. Merchant's Favor is a currency from the supply
# crates turned in at the camps, not gold; its patterns bind when picked up.
#
# Camping: Enchanted Lute (skill 20) is the Enchanting camp item. The Arcane Salvager (skill 140,
# blueprint from Rath'mael, Ruins of Lordaeron) improves disenchanting at a camp and needs the Runed
# Truesilver Rod; the skill-300 Arcane Forge has no known blueprint source.
#
# Ranks: Expert is taught only by Kitta Firewind (Tower of Azora, Elwynn Forest) and Hgarth (Sun
# Rock Retreat, Stonetalon Mountains). Artisan is taught only by Annora inside Uldaman: enter by the
# back door (Badlands), clear the scorpids in her room until she appears, and learn every formula up
# to 250 on that visit. The new starter quests An Enchanting Lesson (Kitta Firewind, Alliance) and A
# Pain in the Neck (Pa'zula, Sen'jin Village, Horde) teach Disenchant on a quest item. Enchanting
# has no specialisation.
#
# Route (crafts are expected counts; yellow and green crafts can take more):
#     1-25  Enchant Bracer - Inferior Stamina, about 31 (known): 1 Mote of Magic each
#    25-75  Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina, about 51 (trainer 50c): 1 Strange Dust each
#    75-90  Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina, about 22 (trainer 50c): 1 Strange Dust each
#    90-130 Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection, about 48 (trainer 2s): 2 Strange Dust each
#   130-150 Enchant Bracer - Lesser Stamina, about 20 (trainer): 1 Soul Dust each
#   150-160 Enchant Bracer - Lesser Stamina, about 11 (trainer): 1 Soul Dust each
#   160-205 Enchant Boots - Lesser Agility, about 59 (trainer): 1 Soul Dust each
#   205-225 Enchant Cloak - Greater Defense, about 20 (trainer): 1 Vision Dust each
#   225-253 Enchant Gloves - Agility, about 39 (trainer): 1 Vision Dust each
#   253-275 Lesser Mana Oil, about 34 (recipe 1g): 1 Dream Dust, 1 Purple Lotus and 1 Crystal Vial each
#   275-300 Enchant Shield - Greater Stamina, about 29 (recipe 1g 20s): 6 Dream Dust each
#
# Shopping per bracket (vendor goods at vendor prices; gathered or dropped materials by count):
# 1-75: Apprentice 10c, recipes 50c, vendor goods 4s 44c; gather or buy 51 Strange Dust.
# 75-150: Journeyman 5s (Classic price), recipes 2s plus unpriced trainer recipes; gather or buy 1
# Shadowgem, 1 Silver Rod, 4 Lesser Magic Essence, 121 Strange Dust and 20 Soul Dust.
# 150-225: Expert 50s (Classic price), trainer recipes (prices not in the data); gather or buy 1
# Iridescent Pearl, 1 Black Pearl, 1 Greater Astral Essence, 71 Soul Dust, 1 Golden Rod, 1 Greater
# Mystic Essence, 21 Vision Dust and 1 Truesilver Rod.
# 225-300: Artisan 5g (Classic price), recipes 2g 20s plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor goods 1g
# 70s; gather or buy 34 Purple Lotus, 39 Vision Dust and 208 Dream Dust.
#
# Data: recipes, colours and reagents from the Forever client's tables; trainer learn skills and
# prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists (they reach skill 50-150); vendors, stock and drops
# from data/forever. Materials are valued at about four times their vendor sell price (cloth and
# leather by the square root of it, hides four times higher; tools/lib/professions/materials.js) to
# rank recipes against each other, never as a price forecast.
# ASSUMED: learn skills of Runed Silver Rod 100, Enchant Bracer - Lesser Stamina 130, Runed Golden
# Rod 150, Enchant Boots - Lesser Agility 160, Runed Truesilver Rod 200, Enchant Cloak - Greater
# Defense 205 and Enchant Gloves - Agility 210 (no sniffed Forever list teaches them: Classic's
# trainer skill moved as far as Forever moved the recipe's colours, which the sniffed lists bear out
# on 126 of 129 recipes). In-game check: the skill the trainer asks; their prices are not in the
# data.
# ASSUMED: rank level gates Journeyman 10, Expert 20 and Artisan 35 (Classic's; Forever's sniffed
# lists ask level 1 for Apprentice). In-game check: the level each trainer asks.
# ASSUMED: rank prices Journeyman 5s, Expert 50s and Artisan 5g (Classic's trainer lists; Forever's
# sniffed lists price only Apprentice, 10c as in Classic). In-game check: what each rank costs.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice (1-75)

step Learn Enchanting
  tip Apprentice Enchanting lets you craft up to 75 for 10c, at any character level. Not every Enchanting trainer teaches it: Alliance Alanna Raveneye (Teldrassil), Betty Quin (Stormwind City), Eaysaa Brightgust (Zephras Isle), Gimble Thistlefuzz (Ironforge), Kitta Firewind (Elwynn Forest), Lalina Summermoon (Darnassus), Lucan Cordell (Stormwind City), Nasalanna Windsinger (Zephras Isle), Taladan (Darnassus), Thonys Pillarstone (Ironforge), Tilli Thistlefuzz (Ironforge) and Xylinnia Starshine (Feralas); Horde Eaysaa Brightgust (Zephras Isle), Godan (Orgrimmar), Hgarth (Stonetalon Mountains), Jhag (Orgrimmar), Lavinia Crowe (Undercity), Malcomb Wynn (Undercity), Mot Dawnstrider (Thunder Bluff), Nasalanna Windsinger (Zephras Isle), Teg Dawnstrider (Thunder Bluff) and Vance Undergloom (Tirisfal Glades). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. Buy a Copper Rod and Mote of Magic from an enchanting supplies vendor (in the capitals and on Zephras Isle; the starting-area trainers have none beside them, and the next step's arrow picks the nearest). From now on, disenchant every green you do not wear: that is where the dust and essences come from. Two starter quests teach Disenchant on a quest item: An Enchanting Lesson from Kitta Firewind (Tower of Azora, Elwynn Forest) and A Pain in the Neck from Pa'zula (Sen'jin Village, Durotar). 1-75 takes about 50c of recipes and 4s 44c of vendor goods, plus 51 Strange Dust to gather or buy.
  train Enchanting Apprentice
  skill Enchanting 1

step Enchanting 1-75: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 1 Copper Rod (1s 24c) and 32 Mote of Magic (3s 20c); about 4s 44c in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Edna Mullby and Jessara Cordell; Orgrimmar: Felika, Kithas and Shimra).
  buy 6217 x1 nearest
  buy 247786 x32 nearest

step Enchant Bracer - Inferior Stamina to 25
  tip Enchant Bracer - Inferior Stamina is orange at 1 (yellow 20, green 22, grey 25): about 31 crafts to 25. Each takes 1 Mote of Magic. One Mote of Magic (10c) a craft; grey at 25 on Forever. Make the Runed Copper Rod first: the recipe needs it in your bags, so keep it there. Enchant any item for that slot in your bags, even a grey one.
  craft 7421 x1 -- a tool: keep it in your bags
  craft 7418 until 25

step Enchanting recipes at 25
  tip Back to an Enchanting trainer: Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina (from 15, 50c). Also learn Enchanted Lute (1s): Forever's Enchanting camp item, 1 Simple Wood and 1 Strange Dust, placed at a campsite beside a campfire for its buff. The Camping 101: Enchanting quest from your starting area's camping guide (after The Great Outdoors) sends you to an enchanting trainer who teaches it free.
  learn 7420
  learn 1230643

step Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina to 75
  tip Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina is orange at 25 (yellow 70, green 90, grey 110): about 51 crafts to 75. Each takes 1 Strange Dust. One Strange Dust a craft: the dust most level 5-20 greens break into, armour above all. Lesser Magic Essence (from weapons) does the same job through Bracer - Minor Deflect or Chest - Minor Absorption if you have more of it. Strange Dust (51 for 1-75): Enchanting: disenchant green items of item level 5-20; or the Auction House. Enchant any item for that slot in your bags, even a grey one.
  craft 7420 until 75
  skill Enchanting 75

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Journeyman (75-150)

step Journeyman Enchanting
  tip Journeyman raises the cap from 75 to 150 for 5s (Classic's price; Forever's is not in the data); it needs Enchanting 50 and character level 10, so you can take it on any visit from 50. Not every Enchanting trainer teaches it: Alliance Gimble Thistlefuzz (Ironforge), Kitta Firewind (Elwynn Forest), Lucan Cordell (Stormwind City), Taladan (Darnassus) and Xylinnia Starshine (Feralas); Horde Godan (Orgrimmar), Hgarth (Stonetalon Mountains), Lavinia Crowe (Undercity) and Teg Dawnstrider (Thunder Bluff). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. Learn now: Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection (from 70, 2s). 75-150 takes about 2s of recipes, plus 1 Shadowgem, 1 Silver Rod, 4 Lesser Magic Essence, 121 Strange Dust and 20 Soul Dust to gather or buy.
  level 10
  train Enchanting Journeyman
  learn 7771

step Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina to 90
  tip Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina is yellow at 75 (yellow 70, green 90, grey 110): about 22 crafts to 90. Each takes 1 Strange Dust. One Strange Dust a craft: the dust most level 5-20 greens break into, armour above all. Lesser Magic Essence (from weapons) does the same job through Bracer - Minor Deflect or Chest - Minor Absorption if you have more of it. Strange Dust (121 for 75-150): Enchanting: disenchant green items of item level 5-20; or the Auction House. Enchant any item for that slot in your bags, even a grey one.
  craft 7420 until 90

step Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection to 130
  tip Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection is orange at 90 (yellow 110, green 130, grey 150): about 48 crafts to 130. Each takes 2 Strange Dust. Two Strange Dust a craft (the trainer teaches it from 70 for 2s); keep disenchanting the greens of the 10-20 zones. Enchant any item for that slot in your bags, even a grey one.
  craft 7771 until 130

step Enchanting recipes at 130
  tip Back to an Enchanting trainer: Runed Silver Rod (from 100) and Enchant Bracer - Lesser Stamina (from 130).
  learn 7795
  learn 13501

step Enchant Bracer - Lesser Stamina to 150
  tip Enchant Bracer - Lesser Stamina is orange at 130 (yellow 155, green 175, grey 195): about 20 crafts to 150, a point every craft. Each takes 1 Soul Dust. One Soul Dust a craft (level 21-30 greens). Make the Runed Silver Rod first: the recipe needs it in your bags, so keep it there. Shadowgem (1 for 75-150): Shadowgem turns up in about one Copper Vein, Tin Vein or Silver Vein in 100: buy it at the Auction House, or keep the ones you find while mining. Silver Rod (1 for 75-150): Blacksmithing: Silver Rod; or the Auction House. Lesser Magic Essence (4 for 75-150): Enchanting: disenchant green items of item level 5-15; or the Auction House. Soul Dust (20 for 75-150): Enchanting: disenchant green items of item level 21-30; or the Auction House. Enchant any item for that slot in your bags, even a grey one. Enchanting 150 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 7795 x1 -- a tool: keep it in your bags
  craft 13501 until 150
  skill Enchanting 150

